From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:20:15 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] tg16-carts

TurboGrafx-16 games sit on the shelf as HuCards: a retro bitmap shell
the size of a Sega Card (both are credit cards), white plastic, grip
ridges at the top, a square label below the middle and a row of gold
contacts under it. The contacts are painted the way the Japanese obi
strip is, in gold, over fingers drawn in the neutral. The label art is
fitted whole into the well. The Logo Only tool takes its system list
from the shelves, so TG16 gets a logo label too.

The HuCard drawing follows nelynes/slotPlus 92b7022 assets/src/carts.py
(GPL-3.0).
